From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] dma-direct: export dma_direct_alloc and dma_direct_free

The gs201 WCN6740 driver (wlan/qcom/wcn6740/cnss2: cnss2.ko and mhi.ko) is
built with -DCONFIG_WCN_USE_DMA_DIRECT and allocates its firmware memory
segments and the MHI BHIe vector table with dma_direct_alloc() /
dma_direct_free(), bypassing any IOMMU on the PCIe link so the firmware sees
physical addresses. The Android 6.1 GKI exported both (an ANDROID: vendor
export); neither ACK 6.18 nor android-mainline does, and the lynx dist fails
in modpost:

  ERROR: modpost: "dma_direct_alloc" [cnss2/cnss2.ko] undefined!
  ERROR: modpost: "dma_direct_free" [mhi/core/mhi.ko] undefined!

Export both, GPL-only, rather than switch the driver to dma_alloc_attrs():
that would change which address space the WLAN firmware is handed, which is
not something to change blind. lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/).

lynx-mainline: rebased onto android-mainline. The 6.18 version also added
both names to gki/aarch64/symbols/pixel, because that build trimmed GKI
exports to the KMI lists; android-mainline has no KMI and no symbol lists,
so that hunk is gone.
---
diff --git a/kernel/dma/direct.c b/kernel/dma/direct.c
index bab7193cf2b8..fd74b1405865 100644
--- a/kernel/dma/direct.c
+++ b/kernel/dma/direct.c
@@ -357,6 +357,7 @@ void *dma_direct_alloc(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 out_leak_pages:
 	return NULL;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dma_direct_alloc);
 
 void dma_direct_free(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 		void *cpu_addr, dma_addr_t dma_addr, unsigned long attrs)
@@ -430,6 +431,7 @@ void dma_direct_free(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 	else
 		dma_free_contiguous(dev, dma_direct_to_page(dev, dma_addr), size);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dma_direct_free);
 
 struct page *dma_direct_alloc_pages(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 		dma_addr_t *dma_handle, enum dma_data_direction dir, gfp_t gfp)
